    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "08e10dc0-4c6c-4a75-a3c8-a2d3fa42fc9e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Target Variable Creation\n",
    "\n",
    "The original Exam_Score is numerical. Since this project is a classification task, the scores were converted into three performance categories:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Low: Exam_Score below 65\n",
    "- Medium: Exam_Score from 65 to 69\n",
    "- High: Exam_Score of 70 or above\n",
    "\n",
    "The Medium class contains more records than the Low and High classes. Therefore, stratified data splitting and class-sensitive evaluation metrics should be used."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "e7358032-af90-4546-9394-236f21a2043e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = df.drop(columns=[\"Exam_Score\", \"Performance\"])\n",
    "y = df[\"Performance\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "a4e59e77-9d37-44fa-bb3c-32ba4607dd08",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "X shape: (6607, 19)\n",
      "y shape: (6607,)\n",
      "Exam_Score in X: False\n",
      "Performance in X: False\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"X shape:\", X.shape)\n",
    "print(\"y shape:\", y.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Exam_Score in X:\", \"Exam_Score\" in X.columns)\n",
    "print(\"Performance in X:\", \"Performance\" in X.columns)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "22f5a558-5f2f-44d7-b6e7-bf8c23f56101",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature and Target Separation\n",
    "\n",
    "The input features are stored in X, while the target variable is stored in y. Exam_Score was removed from X because it was used to create the Performance category. Including Exam_Score would reveal the correct answer to the model and cause target leakage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "f6144690-c778-40dd-9898-7bd1807c0b24",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Hours_Studied                  int64\n",
       "Attendance                     int64\n",
       "Parental_Involvement          object\n",
       "Access_to_Resources           object\n",
       "Extracurricular_Activities    object\n",
       "Sleep_Hours                    int64\n",
       "Previous_Scores                int64\n",
       "Motivation_Level              object\n",
       "Internet_Access               object\n",
       "Tutoring_Sessions              int64\n",
       "Family_Income                 object\n",
       "Teacher_Quality               object\n",
       "School_Type                   object\n",
       "Peer_Influence                object\n",
       "Physical_Activity              int64\n",
       "Learning_Disabilities         object\n",
       "Parental_Education_Level      object\n",
       "Distance_from_Home            object\n",
       "Gender                        object\n",
       "dtype: object"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 15,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X.dtypes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "a78ca7e7-90c3-450a-97a2-0b0a9b53a849",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Numeric features:\n",
      "['Hours_Studied', 'Attendance', 'Sleep_Hours', 'Previous_Scores', 'Tutoring_Sessions', 'Physical_Activity']\n",
      "\n",
      "Categorical features:\n",
      "['Parental_Involvement', 'Access_to_Resources', 'Extracurricular_Activities', 'Motivation_Level', 'Internet_Access', 'Family_Income', 'Teacher_Quality', 'School_Type', 'Peer_Influence', 'Learning_Disabilities', 'Parental_Education_Level', 'Distance_from_Home', 'Gender']\n",
      "\n",
      "Number of numeric features: 6\n",
      "Number of categorical features: 13\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "numeric_features = X.select_dtypes(include=[\"int64\", \"float64\"]).columns.tolist()\n",
    "categorical_features = X.select_dtypes(include=[\"object\", \"category\"]).columns.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Numeric features:\")\n",
    "print(numeric_features)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCategorical features:\")\n",
    "print(categorical_features)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nNumber of numeric features:\", len(numeric_features))\n",
    "print(\"Number of categorical features:\", len(categorical_features))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "563a6501-0116-4ec0-a9a4-3da4e5fb802d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Parental_Involvement : ['Low' 'Medium' 'High']\n",
      "Access_to_Resources : ['High' 'Medium' 'Low']\n",
      "Extracurricular_Activities : ['No' 'Yes']\n",
      "Motivation_Level : ['Low' 'Medium' 'High']\n",
      "Internet_Access : ['Yes' 'No']\n",
      "Family_Income : ['Low' 'Medium' 'High']\n",
      "Teacher_Quality : ['Medium' 'High' 'Low']\n",
      "School_Type : ['Public' 'Private']\n",
      "Peer_Influence : ['Positive' 'Negative' 'Neutral']\n",
      "Learning_Disabilities : ['No' 'Yes']\n",
      "Parental_Education_Level : ['High School' 'College' 'Postgraduate']\n",
      "Distance_from_Home : ['Near' 'Moderate' 'Far']\n",
      "Gender : ['Male' 'Female']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "for column in categorical_features:\n",
    "    print(column, \":\", df[column].dropna().unique())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7b7856ff-d962-45af-a28b-dc54430e1d79",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature Types\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset contains numerical and categorical input features. KNN requires numerical input because it makes predictions using distance calculations. Numerical features will be standardized, while categorical features will be converted using one-hot encoding.\n",
    "\n",
    "One-hot encoding is used to avoid creating artificial numerical distances between nominal categories."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "86c80fed-5882-4042-9c79-0563a516c456",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "48a47cc3-a7d9-4f0f-a3f6-b995b2fee331",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X,\n",
    "    y,\n",
    "    test_size=0.20,\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    stratify=y\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "959d6f97-5504-4771-926e-8a90d032b9b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Training feature shape: (5285, 19)\n",
      "Testing feature shape: (1322, 19)\n",
      "Training target shape: (5285,)\n",
      "Testing target shape: (1322,)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Training feature shape:\", X_train.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Testing feature shape:\", X_test.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Training target shape:\", y_train.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Testing target shape:\", y_test.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "4c7c3dc3-6844-433b-accf-177ed20e6c42",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Training class distribution:\n",
      "Performance\n",
      "Low       0.219678\n",
      "Medium    0.534342\n",
      "High      0.245979\n",
      "Name: proportion, dtype: float64\n",
      "\n",
      "Testing class distribution:\n",
      "Performance\n",
      "Low       0.220121\n",
      "Medium    0.534039\n",
      "High      0.245840\n",
      "Name: proportion, dtype: float64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Training class distribution:\")\n",
    "print(y_train.value_counts(normalize=True).sort_index())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTesting class distribution:\")\n",
    "print(y_test.value_counts(normalize=True).sort_index())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f0fdb6aa-5a48-4181-9716-1d5d1e824fc3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Train-Test Split\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset was divided into 80% training data and 20% testing data. The training set is used to train and select the KNN model, while the testing set is reserved for final evaluation on unseen data.\n",
    "\n",
    "A random state of 42 was used to make the experiment reproducible. Stratified splitting was applied to maintain similar proportions of Low, Medium, and High performance classes in both datasets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "6ebf2600-d6e2-4ca3-a578-c7b4c562acf3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "915f5341-b5eb-423d-9100-d4864831b64f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Numeric features:\n",
      "['Hours_Studied', 'Attendance', 'Sleep_Hours', 'Previous_Scores', 'Tutoring_Sessions', 'Physical_Activity']\n",
      "\n",
      "Categorical features:\n",
      "['Parental_Involvement', 'Access_to_Resources', 'Extracurricular_Activities', 'Motivation_Level', 'Internet_Access', 'Family_Income', 'Teacher_Quality', 'School_Type', 'Peer_Influence', 'Learning_Disabilities', 'Parental_Education_Level', 'Distance_from_Home', 'Gender']\n",
      "\n",
      "Number of numeric features: 6\n",
      "Number of categorical features: 13\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "numeric_features = X_train.select_dtypes(\n",
    "    include=np.number\n",
    ").columns.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "categorical_features = X_train.select_dtypes(\n",
    "    exclude=np.number\n",
    ").columns.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Numeric features:\")\n",
    "print(numeric_features)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCategorical features:\")\n",
    "print(categorical_features)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nNumber of numeric features:\", len(numeric_features))\n",
    "print(\"Number of categorical features:\", len(categorical_features))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 24,
   "id": "5bc9682b-938f-4ac5-ba48-8607dc557b37",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "numeric_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
    "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler())\n",
    "])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "6f22b353-7459-46f2-917a-24e7559139ea",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "categorical_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")),\n",
    "    (\"onehot\", OneHotEncoder(\n",
    "        handle_unknown=\"ignore\",\n",
    "        sparse_output=False\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "af18f2f2-7598-4a6f-b0b6-55899359263d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer([\n",
    "    (\"numeric\", numeric_pipeline, numeric_features),\n",
    "    (\"categorical\", categorical_pipeline, categorical_features)\n",
    "])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 45,
   "id": "4fb824dd-0886-43b6-a365-b17405a87344",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "knn_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"preprocessor\", preprocessor),\n",
    "    (\"knn\", KNeighborsClassifier(\n",
    "        algorithm=\"ball_tree\"\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4910c2b7-9c53-4467-bc24-f6cd596028a7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data Preprocessing Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "A preprocessing pipeline was created to prevent data leakage. Numerical features are imputed using the training-set median and standardized using StandardScaler. Categorical features are imputed using the most frequent training value and converted using one-hot encoding.\n",
    "\n",
    "The preprocessing steps and KNN classifier are combined in one pipeline. Therefore, preprocessing is fitted only on the training data during model training and cross-validation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "963c5f8c-a1e8-466e-9078-858002d44a9e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.dummy import DummyClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, balanced_accuracy_score"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 29,
   "id": "bfc8e016-52d4-40f8-a26f-cf24b4829ee7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "baseline_model = DummyClassifier(\n",
    "    strategy=\"most_frequent\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "baseline_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "baseline_pred = baseline_model.predict(X_test)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "c16750a8-9464-4f61-ae99-fe43ef014ec1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Baseline prediction: ['High' 'Low' 'Medium']\n",
      "Baseline accuracy: 0.5340393343419062\n",
      "Baseline balanced accuracy: 0.3333333333333333\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "baseline_accuracy = accuracy_score(\n",
    "    y_test,\n",
    "    baseline_pred\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "baseline_balanced_accuracy = balanced_accuracy_score(\n",
    "    y_test,\n",
    "    baseline_pred\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Baseline prediction:\", baseline_model.classes_)\n",
    "print(\"Baseline accuracy:\", baseline_accuracy)\n",
    "print(\"Baseline balanced accuracy:\", baseline_balanced_accuracy)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "4456396d-e93e-4371-ab0a-48333d6d718c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Medium    1322\n",
       "Name: count, dtype: int64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 31,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "pd.Series(baseline_pred).value_counts()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "897e7644-156b-482e-a52c-d900a66c96cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Baseline Model\n",
    "\n",
    "A majority-class baseline was created before training KNN. This baseline does not use the student features and always predicts the most frequent training class, which is Medium.\n",
    "\n",
    "The baseline provides a minimum performance reference. The final KNN model should achieve better accuracy and balanced accuracy than this simple prediction rule."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "a8cfad49-312f-43bb-a291-cb3000e506bd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.model_selection import GridSearchCV, StratifiedKFold"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "9191587f-8deb-4684-aaad-dca2bde48061",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "parameter_grid = {\n",
    "    \"knn__n_neighbors\": [3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 15, 21, 31],\n",
    "    \"knn__weights\": [\"uniform\", \"distance\"],\n",
    "    \"knn__p\": [1, 2]\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "f15c73e0-67a0-414e-b415-8cfc6822956d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cross_validation = StratifiedKFold(\n",
    "    n_splits=5,\n",
    "    shuffle=True,\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 46,
   "id": "bf5eaa30-7704-4485-870a-ee6157b8aa01",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "grid_search = GridSearchCV(\n",
    "    estimator=knn_pipeline,\n",
    "    param_grid=parameter_grid,\n",
    "    scoring=\"f1_macro\",\n",
    "    cv=cross_validation,\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1,\n",
    "    verbose=1,\n",
    "    return_train_score=True\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 47,
   "id": "360f5e3a-5f65-45f8-bb10-91bdb3a0b4a4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Fitting 5 folds for each of 32 candidates, totalling 160 fits\n"
     ]
    },
    {
